```java
public E pollFirst() {
    final Object[] es;
    final int h;
    E e = elementAt(es = elements, h = head);
    if (e != null) {
        es[h] = null;
        head = inc(h, es.length);
    }
    return e;
    // @@@ If the deque is empty, then the result is null.
}
```

We need to express that if the deque is empty before operation, then result (\result) is null. Need to refer to old state: empty means size() == 0 before call. So assert: (\old(this.isEmpty())) => \result == null. Or maybe we can use this.size(). Since we have method size(). So we can write:

assert (\old(this.isEmpty())) => \result == null;

But need to ensure we use \old(this.isEmpty()) or \old(this.size() == 0). Use isEmpty().

Thus final answer:

```java
assert (\old(this.isEmpty())) => \result == null;
```

